WEBVTT

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:02.500
This is what it will be.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.900
In the upcoming Champion Carnival,

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.140
our gym's Junior Lightweight
boxer, Kimura Tatsuya...

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.900
will be fighting in his first Japan Title match.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.770
Th-this is it.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.540
Because Kimura-san and Kumi-san's
brother will be facing off...

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.610
back then...

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.680
I'm sorry.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.520
I don't think I can I see you anymore.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.660
Wh-why?

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:30.590
How come?

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:31.860
Well, goodbye.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:32.760
Kumi-san...

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.600
N-no...

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.600
but there was nothing I could do.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.890
I just have to...

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.500
Good luck, Kimura-san.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.100
Don't force yourself.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.710
You were getting along fine with her...

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.510
sorry for ruining it.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.440
I'll beat the hell out of that brother,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.650
and oust him from his throne!

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.950
Th-that's the spirit.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.290
Mashiba Ryo
Kimura Tatsuya

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.650
I knew I would find you if I waited here.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.050
I need a favor.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.580
Please help me.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.150
Why the sudden request?

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.160
I've got a match scheduled.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.490
No matter what, I want to win.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.600
But... right now, there's nothing I can do.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.460
What do you want from me?

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.670
I'm not the sort who trains others.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:51.610
Besides, you have no weak points, and
come across as a high-level boxer.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.110
But,

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.280
I know for sure...

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.110
I can't win against him.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:01:59.610
Him?

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.280
The Japan Junior Lightweight Class Champion...

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.120
Mashiba Ryo.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.790
For the Champion Carnival,

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:13.130
the 1st and 2nd ranked boxers bailed.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:16.400
So the baton was passed down
to me, the 3rd ranked boxer.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.470
In my 5th year as a boxer,

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.470
this chance has finally come.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.240
If I let this pass,

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.870
I might never have another chance like this.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:25.950
I want to win this!

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:27.780
Miyata.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.280
Your technique and speed
are superior to Mashiba's.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.110
If I can spar evenly against
you, I'll be in perfect form!

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.010
I don't know...

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.020
I don't think I can meet your expectations.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.290
And like I said,

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.990
I'm not the sort who trains others.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:46.060
I...

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:49.660
I've never stuck to any single thing for long.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.170
My record isn't impressive, but...

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.030
I've been putting in my best.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.270
I love boxing.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.210
That's why...

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.860
I want to be confident in not losing to anyone in it.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.650
I want proof that I've tried my best in what I love.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.920
You mean, the belt?

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:12.920
That's right.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.760
Sorry for wasting your time.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.400
I'm heading back.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:26.800
Kimura-san.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:31.210
I have an OPBF Title match next year.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.840
And the Champion is an out-boxer.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.950
His fighting style is similar to yours.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:41.920
If you spar with me, it would be helpful.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:45.290
If you'd like...

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.650
please visit my gym tomorrow.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.030
Trying to act cool?

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.430
Alright!

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:00.170
Do you think Miyata-kun accepted his request?

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.200
No matter who trains him, the
outcome will be the same.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.170
Kimura-san is very proficient.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.280
We won't know for sure until he actually tries.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.510
W-well, for him to face Mashiba...

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.020
is somewhat unfortunate, I guess.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.380
Unfortunate?

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.750
Is the unfortunate one really Kimura?

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:24.730
Mashiba-san and my Senpai are fighting each other.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.390
And, I'm in love with his sister.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.160
Torn between two opposing sides, I...

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.160
I am so unfortunate!

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.800
So, that's what you think, right?!

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:38.110
But...

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.370
there's another who's more nervous than you.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.050
Aoki-san??

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.060
Aoki and Kimura joined at the same time.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:55.060
In a sense, they're each others' best rivals.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.560
And his rival is facing his first title match.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:01.100
Being left behind isn't what's bothering him.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.570
Actually, it's the exact opposite.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:06.070
He's frustrated at his inability; to help...

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.940
even though he wants to.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:26.750
Damn it...

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:34.430
Now that you're sparring with Ichiro,

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.660
be on your guard.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.430
Got it.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:46.310
Every single movement of his will help me.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.910
And when I can overcome those moves...

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:51.870
Mashiba's Flicker will no longer be a threat.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:56.520
Now then, let's get started,

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:57.920
on neutralizing the Flicker.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:58.950
The Flicker...

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.020
like this?

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.380
Fast...

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:08.060
Mine is slightly different, but...

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.700
I can use the Flicker.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:10.530
Good!

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:11.870
Use it, then.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:14.440
Once I get used to them, a Flicker
neutralizer can be found.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.470
It's impossible.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.040
Despite its power,

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.070
the Flicker is just a jab.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.080
It's almost impossible to stop all the jabs.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:24.080
Actually...

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.980
even if you evade them all,
you can't defeat Mashiba.

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:28.880
Wh-what do you mean?

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.450
You have a critical weak point.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:32.920
What?

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.160
For a start, let's make you aware of it.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:41.430
My weakness?

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.070
He's fast.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:48.340
But we're both out-boxers.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.130
I can predict his moves somewhat.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:57.950
I can hit him.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:58.850
I can do it!

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:01.350
Nice movement.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:05.990
He's ranked 3rd yet his potential exceeds that.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:06.860
However...

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.020
Weren't you a little hard on him for the first day?

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.990
I wanted him to experience it.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:44.120
E-experience it?

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.190
Are you okay?

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:47.160
If you come at me with full force,

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:48.830
I can't tell what's going on.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:49.830
That's the point.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:53.370
You're so well rounded that

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:55.940
I don't see any flaws.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.160
On the other hand...

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:59.710
you don't display any strengths either.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.810
In addition, you don't have a finishing blow.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:06.380
Without one, your opponent won't
hesitate to close in on you.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.020
There's nothing to fear.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.720
Mashiba probably thinks the same of you.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:14.220
Damn it.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.860
When he attacked so aggressively,

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:17.620
it became so damn hard.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:20.660
I knew about it...

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.960
my own weakness.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.970
He didn't hold back.

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:33.070
You don't seem to have any worries.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:46.820
There must be something...

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.720
Some kind of strategy to defeat Mashiba.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:08:59.900
Welcome!

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:00.850
Yo.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:05.340
You look like you're getting trashed.

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:06.470
Well, yeah.

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:10.010
I need to start dieting soon, so
I'm stuffing myself for now.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:11.780
Are a Stamina Ramen and a Gyoza enough?

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.110
Your treat.

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:39.910
Thanks.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:41.910
As usual, it was good.

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:42.890
Of course.

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:48.600
Hey, umm...

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.750
it's nothing...

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.860
What, feeling blue?

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:56.660
Hell no!

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:58.660
I was gonna say that I've become stronger!

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.300
If we spar now, you'll be dead in one minute.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.300
I'll just return the favor!

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:14.880
See ya.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:15.810
Yeah.

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:28.980
Thank you very much.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:33.030
What was that about?

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:37.560
I borrowed some recent videos on
Mashiba-san from Iimura-san.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:39.670
I want to help Kimura-san in some way.

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:40.370
All right.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:41.990
Leave their delivery to me.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.200
Thank you.

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.710
You're pretty thoughtful.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:48.240
Actually...

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:51.180
I spent the whole night coming
up with advice for Kimura.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:52.410
You did?

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:54.350
For the Mashiba match?

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.550
I can be thoughtful too.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:58.250
If that's the case, I'll pass it on.

00:10:58.250 --> 00:10:59.890
Yeah, sure.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.020
Watch out for...

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:05.630
Mashiba's long reach.

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:07.130
Well, see you later.

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:08.760
Thanks.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:11.700
Now then...

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:23.010
Yo, long time no see.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:24.830
Are ambushes becoming popular?

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:27.370
Oh, I'm just making a delivery.

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.720
They're recent videos of Mashiba...

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:33.850
for your reference.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:35.990
Well, that's all.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:43.390
Can... Kimura win?

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.770
Please tell me!

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:51.710
You can tell, right?

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:54.440
Please, Miyata.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.310
Say something.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.070
I'm not a critic.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:05.070
He considers this title match his last chance.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:07.080
His last?

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.080
He must be thinking of retiring.

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:15.560
We're already 23 years old.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.770
We've been boxing for 5 years.

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:20.230
We've fought over 16 matches.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:22.400
People may consider us young, but...

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.910
as active boxers, we're not.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:27.780
We've also let many chances slip away.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:31.520
Please.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:34.520
Please, Miyata!

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:36.820
I'm not asking for a definite victory.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:37.950
But, at least...

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:41.490
at least let him have a fight with no regrets.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.820
Polish him so he can at least do that.

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:46.260
Don't let him have any regrets.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:48.230
Please!

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:58.610
I'll be sure to pass these to him.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:21.900
Mashiba's basic pattern hasn't changed.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:24.630
But his stamina has improved.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.430
His diet regimen isn't as tough,
after moving up a weight class.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.600
If he uses Flickers for 10 rounds,

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:31.660
you can't get close to him.

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:33.640
In my present form,

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:36.210
I wonder if I can even defeat him with out-boxing.

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:38.410
My chances are even slimmer.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.180
The difference in reach is too great.

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:42.720
My jabs are just no match for his.

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:45.290
Isn't there something...

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:47.050
that annoys out-boxers?

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.060
Something hard to handle...

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:51.230
Hard to handle?

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:53.490
When he attacked so aggressively

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.200
it became so damn hard.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:13:59.730
What is it?

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:01.070
N-nothing.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:07.240
From now on, I'll step in more aggressively!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.200
Improve my head-slip.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.350
Make it faster.

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:39.440
That way... I can get closer to him.

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:46.610
Mashiba...

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.380
Mashiba.

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:52.620
Your tickets will go on sale soon right?

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.420
Can you get 20 good seats for us please?

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:56.080
We'll come to watch you.

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:59.090
Working with a champion...

00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:00.560
somehow makes us feel proud.

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.130
I'll get them.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.870
Come to watch me?

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.670
Looks like you're doing well.

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:14.850
At this rate, there's nothing to worry about.

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:18.350
I'm never one of your worries.

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:21.280
I still worry occasionally.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.110
That's because...

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:28.590
the World has come knocking at our door.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.070
The World?

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:33.110
The WBC 5th ranker wants to fight you.
[ WBC = World Boxing Council ]

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:36.860
If you win that match, the World
title will be within reach.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.370
But we've got to clear your title defense match first.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:41.900
If your victory isn't a decisive one,

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:43.500
the offer will be withdrawn.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:49.010
Really?

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:57.890
I won't lose.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.120
I'll keep on winning,

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:01.860
and make everyone kneel before me,

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.020
my enemies and everyone in the world.

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:08.000
Sounds like you've included me...

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:09.760
but that's fine for now.

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:12.240
That fearlessness...

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.500
is the source of your strength.

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.940
But then you will come to a realization.

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:21.740
I'm sure you will.

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:23.110
Once you keep on winning...

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:25.250
once you reach the tap of the world...

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.020
what will change won't be the world

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:30.220
but you.

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:41.730
I-I got in...

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:43.200
I got in.

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:44.480
I finally got close to you!

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:46.500
This is it.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:50.100
This way, I'll get to close to Mashiba then I'll...

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.540
Then I'll...

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.490
What should I do?

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:57.540
You must have been practicing a lot.

00:16:57.550 --> 00:17:00.450
Similarly, you can surely get close to Mashiba.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.220
When you get close to him...

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:06.690
What the hell?

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:09.520
I don't have any...

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:11.330
weapons...

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:13.510
at all.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:17.200
Miyata must have known about this.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:20.510
That's why he didn't advise me to be an in-fighter.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:23.600
And I was finally getting used to it.

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:25.520
Without a weapon it won't make a difference.

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:27.690
Damn it!

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.140
Think.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:31.550
Think hard.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:33.950
Out-boxing won't work against him.

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:36.570
Get close to him, and then what?

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:38.750
His chin or his body?

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:40.120
His chin, of course.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.590
Mashiba's pointy chin...

00:17:41.590 --> 00:17:44.620
is just about his only weakness.

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:48.160
But I probably can't hit it on my .first try.

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.260
Above all, he's tall.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:53.400
Connecting a punch that high will be hard.

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:55.670
But I need a weapon now!

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:03.350
I'll feed you now.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.890
What an amazing jump!

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:15.090
You can reach that height?

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:22.100
This high...

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:24.300
Arched all the way...

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.500
All the way up here.

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:54.630
What?

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:57.000
You haven't shown up for 2 weeks.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:59.650
We've found another sparring partner.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:02.140
We don't need you any more.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:03.160
Actually, Dad...

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:06.660
it is he, who needs me.

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:14.150
The atmosphere now is different.

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:17.050
Kimura-san is looking for something.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:18.890
But what IS it?

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:20.050
What is he looking for?

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:41.240
What is this...

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.410
this feeling?!

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:48.880
Crap!

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.300
It's no good...

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:07.200
It was countered...

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:08.540
It wasn't countered.

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:13.210
A random punch just happened to hit you.

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:16.380
If that punch was more polished...

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:18.860
the one looking down wouldn't be me.

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:21.360
And, without a doubt...

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:23.120
Mashiba wouldn't either.

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:30.880
What a nice poster!

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:31.290
The Execution
What a nice poster!

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:34.870
The Execution

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:37.460
That catch-phrase is the best!

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:40.000
Kimura's back looks the coolest!

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.640
You don't have to laugh that much.

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:49.240
The Execution

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:53.390
I thought it was weird when the guy was
taking so many pictures of my back.
The Execution

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:53.410
I thought it was weird when the guy was
taking so many pictures of my back.

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:56.420
I know I haven't mastered everything
Miyata taught me,

00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:59.420
but I didn't expect the poster to turn out like this.

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:01.690
You're gonna get executed.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:04.290
Aren't you even annoyed by this?

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:06.190
Bring it on.

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:07.410
However...

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:10.910
the one who will be executed is Mashiba.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:12.910
Do you have a strategy?

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:16.370
Strategy... or, rather...

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:17.920
a finishing blow.

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:20.920
Well, I could call it...

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:23.670
the Dragon Fish Blow.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:26.710
Dragon Fish Blow?

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.420
It's not perfect yet.

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:30.380
I just need to polish it.

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:33.090
Lend me a hand, Aoki, Ippo.

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:34.760
Yeah, you can count on me!

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:35.640
Let's do it!

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:38.130
Takamura-san you too, please.

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:40.390
A dragon fish...

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:41.610
a fishy dragon...

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:43.400
Is it a surprise punch attack?!

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:44.730
Alright.

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:45.730
Let's practice.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:46.800
Let's do it.

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:53.570
Are you sure that's all you're
going to have for dinner?

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.540
I'm on a dieting regime.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.610
I'm going for a run.

00:21:56.610 --> 00:21:58.370
Eat your dinner while I'm at it.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:03.630
Whenever I'm dieting, you hesitate to eat.

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:06.120
You won't be fighting in the match.

00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:11.290
The match is drawing close.

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:12.140
Good luck.

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:16.160
I guess he is your friend, but I won't hold back.

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:18.140
I can't lose.

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:21.540
I know.

00:22:21.540 --> 00:22:22.740
It's a match.

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:23.650
You can't help it.

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.640
Kumi, watch me.

00:22:28.640 --> 00:22:30.810
I'll keep on rising.

00:22:30.810 --> 00:22:35.150
I'll be the World's best brother, and
one that you can be proud of.

00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:44.930
The day of the match

00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:55.390
Well, I'm off.

00:22:55.940 --> 00:22:57.140
Good luck.

00:22:57.140 --> 00:22:57.940
Tatsuya.

00:22:57.940 --> 00:23:00.140
If you win today, you'll be Japan's best, right?

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:03.140
Well yeah... I guess.

00:23:03.140 --> 00:23:04.980
But not yet.

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:06.860
Once we close shop, we'll come to watch you.

00:23:08.120 --> 00:23:08.980
Sure.

00:23:10.290 --> 00:23:12.920
By the way, what flowers are those?

00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:14.590
They're Cinerarias.

00:23:14.590 --> 00:23:15.760
Why the question?

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:20.460
Well, I should start learning the flower's names,

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:22.880
otherwise I won't be able to
help out with the business.

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:33.140
The Execution

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:42.120
Hey, Ippo.

00:23:42.150 --> 00:23:44.280
Have you ever wondered...

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:48.460
Since Kimura and I normally weigh the same,

00:23:48.460 --> 00:23:51.160
why are we in different weight classes?

00:23:52.330 --> 00:23:56.630
You were trying to avoid fighting each other, right?

00:23:58.070 --> 00:23:59.470
Before the pro-test,

00:23:59.470 --> 00:24:02.240
Kimura said that he'd go for Junior Light Title.

00:24:02.240 --> 00:24:04.670
I thought nothing of it.

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:09.740
But, just before the match, the dieting was tough.

00:24:09.740 --> 00:24:11.880
A Lightweight like me found it hard.

00:24:12.310 --> 00:24:14.050
It was even harder for Kimura.

00:24:15.280 --> 00:24:20.350
He never bitched about it.

00:24:20.360 --> 00:24:23.350
Each victory came with double the effort.

00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:26.990
B-but, if that's the case...

00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:29.430
each victory should bring twice the joy.

00:24:30.470 --> 00:24:32.070
Yeah, you're right.

00:24:32.070 --> 00:24:34.410
Especially for a title match.

00:24:35.240 --> 00:24:37.410
If he wins the belt...

00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:40.970
He will do it, I'm sure!

00:24:40.980 --> 00:24:43.840
I want him to be the champion!

00:24:43.850 --> 00:24:45.420
It's about time.

00:25:02.030 --> 00:25:03.000
What's wrong?

00:25:07.540 --> 00:25:10.900
I was thinking about Mashiba's
eyes during the weight check.

00:25:12.170 --> 00:25:14.400
Those eyes don't belong to a human.

00:25:15.510 --> 00:25:17.850
You're scared now?

00:25:17.850 --> 00:25:19.150
Come on, man!

00:25:19.150 --> 00:25:21.850
No matter what eyes he has, Mashiba's still human!

00:25:29.960 --> 00:25:30.920
Coach.

00:25:31.590 --> 00:25:32.670
Everyone.

00:25:33.260 --> 00:25:35.860
I have something to tell you.

00:25:35.860 --> 00:25:37.030
Go ahead.

00:25:37.730 --> 00:25:40.400
In every match I had,

00:25:40.400 --> 00:25:43.670
I thought that I had trained to my limits.

00:25:43.670 --> 00:25:45.770
But, I was wrong.

00:25:45.770 --> 00:25:47.170
I was too easy on myself,

00:25:47.180 --> 00:25:48.690
and was convinced that I put in my all.

00:25:49.740 --> 00:25:53.190
This time, I've overcome that limit.

00:25:53.520 --> 00:25:57.180
So whatever the outcome, there'll be no regrets.

00:25:57.190 --> 00:25:59.950
Actually, I will be satisfied.

00:26:02.220 --> 00:26:03.220
If I lose...

00:26:04.990 --> 00:26:05.910
I will retire.

00:26:10.470 --> 00:26:12.330
K-Kimura-san!

00:26:13.840 --> 00:26:15.470
Why?

00:26:15.470 --> 00:26:16.670
Don't say any more.

00:26:17.010 --> 00:26:19.740
You've been with the gym for 5 years.

00:26:19.740 --> 00:26:22.610
Making such a decision now may be timely.

00:26:22.610 --> 00:26:25.450
Kimura, it's your decision.

00:26:25.450 --> 00:26:28.580
I've been watching you for these past 5 years.

00:26:28.580 --> 00:26:30.820
Show me everything you've got today.

00:26:30.820 --> 00:26:32.350
Against one of Japan's best champions,

00:26:32.350 --> 00:26:34.560
give it all of your 5 years of experience.

00:26:35.820 --> 00:26:36.920
Fight!

00:26:36.930 --> 00:26:38.460
When you step back in here,

00:26:38.460 --> 00:26:39.990
you will be the champion.

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:42.260
I'll be one of your Seconds.

00:26:42.260 --> 00:26:44.530
Leave everything to me!

00:26:48.600 --> 00:26:49.770
Kimura-san...

00:26:51.840 --> 00:26:54.040
Don't look so disappointed.

00:26:56.180 --> 00:26:58.380
I'll only retire if I lose.

00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:05.350
If I win, I'll keep going.

00:27:08.160 --> 00:27:09.620
5 years...

00:27:09.620 --> 00:27:13.530
16 matches 12 wins 8 K.O. 3 losses and 1 draw.

00:27:14.460 --> 00:27:16.630
All of that has lead to this.

00:27:17.770 --> 00:27:19.370
I can't stop shaking.

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:21.100
It's only natural.

00:27:21.900 --> 00:27:23.370
It's not because I'm scared.

00:27:24.340 --> 00:27:27.680
It's because this is my first title match.

00:27:27.680 --> 00:27:28.780
Here I come,

00:27:28.780 --> 00:27:29.910
my dream stage.

00:27:30.750 --> 00:27:32.450
My dream of dreams...

00:27:32.450 --> 00:27:34.310
the title match ring!

00:27:41.390 --> 00:27:42.460
They're staring so hard at each other.

00:27:42.460 --> 00:27:43.960
Their foreheads are almost touching.

00:27:43.960 --> 00:27:45.230
They actually are!

00:27:45.230 --> 00:27:46.930
Don't look away!

00:27:46.930 --> 00:27:48.720
Mashiba, kill him with your glare!

00:27:49.130 --> 00:27:52.030
Hey, hey, trying to act tough?

00:27:52.030 --> 00:27:54.940
He actually looks surprisingly calm.

00:27:55.100 --> 00:27:58.270
M-Miyata-kun, what do you think of this match?

00:27:58.270 --> 00:27:58.940
My guess?

00:28:00.180 --> 00:28:03.480
If Kimura-san can draw out his usual potential,

00:28:03.480 --> 00:28:04.820
it will be interesting.

00:28:05.850 --> 00:28:07.330
You're right.

00:28:07.820 --> 00:28:09.750
They head back to their corners.

00:28:09.750 --> 00:28:12.080
All that's left is the sounding of the gong.

00:28:13.020 --> 00:28:14.390
It's an intense moment.

00:28:14.390 --> 00:28:16.760
What will the judgment be?

00:28:16.760 --> 00:28:17.730
A death sentence?

00:28:17.730 --> 00:28:19.710
Or a comeback verdict of "not guilty"?

00:28:20.130 --> 00:28:21.800
And now, the gong...

00:28:23.160 --> 00:28:24.430
has sounded!

00:28:25.800 --> 00:28:26.930
Tatsuya!

00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:30.500
The challenger comes out of his corner,

00:28:30.510 --> 00:28:32.410
and charges straight for the Japan title.

00:28:36.240 --> 00:28:38.750
And the champion starts up
his unique Hit Man style.

00:28:38.750 --> 00:28:41.690
His Death Scythe sways back and forth.

00:28:41.690 --> 00:28:42.950
The jabs will come.

00:28:42.950 --> 00:28:44.180
I have to evade them.

00:28:44.190 --> 00:28:45.950
Recall your spars against Miyata.

00:28:48.660 --> 00:28:50.200
Good it missed me.

00:28:52.360 --> 00:28:53.960
The champion's left!

00:28:54.400 --> 00:28:56.360
The line of his punch changed.

00:28:56.360 --> 00:28:57.710
I have to keep moving.

00:28:59.400 --> 00:29:01.500
The challenger sways his body,

00:29:01.500 --> 00:29:05.410
but he takes a fierce rush of
the champion's Flickers!

00:29:05.970 --> 00:29:07.890
Wh-what a left.

00:29:08.280 --> 00:29:11.250
Certainly I don't stand a chance in out-boxing.

00:29:12.310 --> 00:29:14.080
He must have realized...

00:29:14.080 --> 00:29:15.850
the threat of Mashiba's reach.

00:29:15.850 --> 00:29:16.900
It was the same for me.

00:29:17.190 --> 00:29:19.390
Seeing and experiencing them are totally different.

00:29:19.390 --> 00:29:21.090
There's no time to complain.

00:29:21.090 --> 00:29:22.900
He has to do something about it.

00:29:24.530 --> 00:29:25.910
I've got to do it.

00:29:25.910 --> 00:29:28.130
Even if I fail at first, I'll keep on trying.

00:29:28.130 --> 00:29:29.410
I'll surely get close to him!

00:29:30.500 --> 00:29:32.410
He's doing that again.

00:29:32.830 --> 00:29:34.910
I heard that he's an out-boxer.

00:29:34.910 --> 00:29:37.170
Yet he's courting an in-fight.

00:29:37.870 --> 00:29:39.170
Be my guest.

00:29:39.340 --> 00:29:41.380
Go ahead if you can.

00:29:42.510 --> 00:29:44.480
Wow, he can't move forward!

00:29:44.880 --> 00:29:46.710
I told you not to be so aggressive!

00:29:46.720 --> 00:29:47.890
Keep your rhythm, your rhythm!

00:29:48.320 --> 00:29:49.520
Trying to come in like a kamikaze?

00:29:49.520 --> 00:29:51.430
What good can a half-assed in-fighter do?

00:29:51.490 --> 00:29:53.790
You can't get me with that.

00:29:53.790 --> 00:29:54.960
My left...

00:29:54.960 --> 00:29:55.980
isn't that easy to get by!

00:29:57.190 --> 00:29:58.980
He's trapped against the ropes!

00:29:58.980 --> 00:30:00.190
Crap!

00:30:00.190 --> 00:30:01.690
Get away, Kimura!

00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:03.860
He got away!

00:30:03.870 --> 00:30:05.900
He narrowly escapes a pinch.

00:30:06.870 --> 00:30:08.450
Th-the challenger's face is...

00:30:13.980 --> 00:30:16.460
Mashiba's left has a lot of snap.

00:30:16.880 --> 00:30:18.710
Each and every punch lacks weight behind it,

00:30:18.710 --> 00:30:19.960
but they cause swelling.

00:30:20.480 --> 00:30:22.420
If he takes more hits, his eyes will swell shut.

00:30:22.420 --> 00:30:23.960
I-if that happens...

00:30:23.960 --> 00:30:25.350
Use your legs!

00:30:25.350 --> 00:30:28.160
Use jabs and regain your rhythm!

00:30:28.160 --> 00:30:29.720
Did you hear that?

00:30:29.720 --> 00:30:32.960
Don't push yourself and fight in your usual style.

00:30:32.960 --> 00:30:34.130
Pity...

00:30:34.130 --> 00:30:36.330
that won't work on me either!

00:30:36.930 --> 00:30:38.630
The challenger doesn't back away!

00:30:38.630 --> 00:30:39.900
He charges in!

00:30:39.900 --> 00:30:41.500
Dodge it.

00:30:41.500 --> 00:30:43.190
Still sticking with in-fighting?

00:30:43.510 --> 00:30:45.110
He is caught!

00:30:45.610 --> 00:30:47.190
Again, the champion's scythe...

00:30:47.190 --> 00:30:49.510
slices up the challenger's face!

00:30:49.700 --> 00:30:51.150
That won't work!

00:30:51.150 --> 00:30:52.610
The challenger backs away.

00:30:52.610 --> 00:30:54.520
Is this all he's got?

00:30:55.020 --> 00:30:56.700
H-he's hurt.

00:30:57.490 --> 00:30:58.190
Now's his chance.

00:30:58.950 --> 00:31:00.710
Mashiba hasn't used his right yet.

00:31:01.490 --> 00:31:03.960
He's using his left to control the match.

00:31:04.330 --> 00:31:06.830
With his right, he can end the match quickly.

00:31:06.830 --> 00:31:07.420
But why?

00:31:08.030 --> 00:31:10.470
Clearly, he has the World stage in sight.

00:31:11.090 --> 00:31:13.530
That bastard's using Kimura as a test.

00:31:13.640 --> 00:31:15.100
A test?

00:31:15.100 --> 00:31:16.400
That's to our advantage.

00:31:16.400 --> 00:31:18.210
If he's relying on the Flicker alone,

00:31:18.210 --> 00:31:19.710
he only has to get its timing down.

00:31:19.710 --> 00:31:20.610
B-but...

00:31:20.610 --> 00:31:22.690
learning that in a match is impossible!

00:31:22.980 --> 00:31:25.400
Can't you see Kimura-san's eyes from here?

00:31:29.150 --> 00:31:31.990
The punches are as swift and sharp as Miyata's.

00:31:32.820 --> 00:31:34.620
What's different is the angle.

00:31:34.620 --> 00:31:36.020
If I can get the right angle...

00:31:36.360 --> 00:31:37.460
I dodged it!

00:31:38.660 --> 00:31:40.960
Wow, a clean hit connected!

00:31:41.360 --> 00:31:43.960
Will he go down?!

00:31:45.230 --> 00:31:47.300
He hung on!

00:31:48.100 --> 00:31:50.870
The 1st round ends with a score of 10-9!

00:31:50.870 --> 00:31:53.180
The Champion wins the first round.

00:31:53.640 --> 00:31:55.780
Damn, that was close.

00:31:55.780 --> 00:31:56.980
Too close!

00:32:01.350 --> 00:32:04.690
You survived well for three minutes.

00:32:04.690 --> 00:32:06.520
Three minutes?

00:32:07.420 --> 00:32:10.120
Only three minutes... that's nothing.

00:32:10.130 --> 00:32:13.700
I've been hanging on for 5 years.

00:32:17.100 --> 00:32:18.270
Are you all right?

00:32:18.270 --> 00:32:19.970
You were taking a lot of hits.

00:32:19.970 --> 00:32:21.670
Don't get so worked up.

00:32:21.670 --> 00:32:24.570
He's actually strong against in-fighters too.

00:32:24.570 --> 00:32:26.770
Let's change our strategy now.

00:32:27.880 --> 00:32:31.850
I didn't expect to get close to him in the first round.

00:32:31.850 --> 00:32:33.680
Let's take it to the full 10 rounds.

00:32:33.680 --> 00:32:35.050
But still...

00:32:35.720 --> 00:32:37.680
Sure, he's good.

00:32:37.680 --> 00:32:40.750
But, he's not beyond my expectations.

00:32:40.760 --> 00:32:41.990
Just watch.

00:32:44.460 --> 00:32:45.660
SECONDS OUT!

00:32:46.400 --> 00:32:48.900
You've been hanging on for 5 years?

00:32:49.630 --> 00:32:52.470
Do you know why I am called the "Executioner"?

00:32:52.470 --> 00:32:56.600
Because 6 boxers have retired after fighting me.

00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:59.970
And... you'll be the 7th!

00:33:04.250 --> 00:33:05.210
He doesn't stand a chance.

00:33:05.850 --> 00:33:06.460
That can't be!

00:33:06.920 --> 00:33:09.020
He can't even get one shot in.

00:33:09.650 --> 00:33:11.460
But he's trying so hard.

00:33:12.250 --> 00:33:13.380
Just like a replay,

00:33:13.420 --> 00:33:16.920
the challenger shows no difference in each round.

00:33:16.930 --> 00:33:18.790
The only difference is his face.

00:33:19.290 --> 00:33:22.930
The moment of his execution draws near.

00:33:23.970 --> 00:33:24.890
Tatsuya!

00:33:28.370 --> 00:33:29.900
He's down!

00:33:29.900 --> 00:33:33.170
The challenger takes this match's first down!

00:33:33.900 --> 00:33:36.280
That took my left 6 rounds.

00:33:36.280 --> 00:33:37.950
That was longer than I expected.

00:33:38.310 --> 00:33:39.480
Kimura-kun...

00:33:44.590 --> 00:33:45.920
He's up!

00:33:45.920 --> 00:33:48.420
The challenger barely stood up!

00:33:49.720 --> 00:33:52.920
And, the 6th round ends here!

00:33:56.830 --> 00:33:57.930
Kimura-san.

00:33:58.330 --> 00:33:59.760
Tatsuya-kun got up.

00:34:00.770 --> 00:34:03.170
Yagi-san, Tatsuya...

00:34:04.390 --> 00:34:05.110
Are you okay?

00:34:05.110 --> 00:34:05.670
He went astray...
Are you okay?

00:34:05.670 --> 00:34:06.640
Can you still see?
He went astray...

00:34:07.110 --> 00:34:09.540
because of me.

00:34:10.580 --> 00:34:13.050
It was when he was in 5th grade.

00:34:14.120 --> 00:34:16.050
He was bullied by an upperclassman,

00:34:16.050 --> 00:34:18.390
and came home all beat up.

00:34:18.950 --> 00:34:21.160
We went to his house to complain.

00:34:21.660 --> 00:34:25.030
But we were pressured by them.

00:34:25.030 --> 00:34:27.160
And I ended up apologizing instead.

00:34:27.160 --> 00:34:28.960
It was then,

00:34:28.960 --> 00:34:31.470
that his impression of his parents changed.

00:34:31.470 --> 00:34:33.530
Time after time, he rebelled.

00:34:33.540 --> 00:34:35.140
By the time he made it to junior high,

00:34:35.140 --> 00:34:38.180
violence at home was an everyday affair.

00:34:39.040 --> 00:34:39.930
SECONDS OUT!

00:34:39.930 --> 00:34:42.810
He was a menace to society.

00:34:42.810 --> 00:34:45.250
Unaware to us, he quit high school.

00:34:45.250 --> 00:34:46.930
He then became uncontrollable.

00:34:47.220 --> 00:34:51.120
But one day, he stopped his violence.

00:34:54.490 --> 00:34:56.490
We were so relieved.

00:34:57.390 --> 00:35:00.320
I wished for him to continue like that.

00:35:00.320 --> 00:35:02.560
Yes, he's working hard.

00:35:03.330 --> 00:35:05.930
Once uncontrollable,

00:35:05.930 --> 00:35:09.830
his fists now challenge the Japan Champion.

00:35:10.240 --> 00:35:12.910
My son's fists have grown great.

00:35:16.950 --> 00:35:19.850
I... was about to make the same mistake again

00:35:21.150 --> 00:35:24.020
by forsaking my duties as his parent.

00:35:24.020 --> 00:35:25.920
Mom, let's go back!

00:35:25.920 --> 00:35:27.060
Y-yes.

00:35:30.930 --> 00:35:32.990
He's taking it to an in-fight!

00:35:33.330 --> 00:35:34.520
T-Tatsuya!

00:35:35.900 --> 00:35:37.730
The champion looks annoyed!

00:35:38.170 --> 00:35:39.650
We're already in the 7th round.

00:35:39.870 --> 00:35:42.840
If this drags on I won't see the World stage.

00:35:43.410 --> 00:35:44.780
Wh-why?

00:35:45.910 --> 00:35:48.880
Why has he suddenly started to evade them all?

00:35:48.880 --> 00:35:50.440
It's his footwork.

00:35:51.210 --> 00:35:52.290
Watch closely.

00:35:53.450 --> 00:35:55.080
With his left foot, his right body moves in.

00:35:55.540 --> 00:35:58.260
Where he just stepped in to stop the jabs,

00:35:58.260 --> 00:36:00.510
is the best place for a left body blow.

00:36:02.510 --> 00:36:04.530
But, why now?

00:36:04.530 --> 00:36:06.490
If you could do that, you should've
done it from the start!

00:36:06.490 --> 00:36:07.970
He was waiting.

00:36:08.460 --> 00:36:11.480
Because of his rushes, Mashiba's speed is slowing.

00:36:11.900 --> 00:36:13.500
While you were hit around like a sand bag,

00:36:13.500 --> 00:36:14.730
you were waiting?

00:36:15.060 --> 00:36:17.300
Kimura is a very clever boxer.

00:36:17.310 --> 00:36:18.770
Very often,

00:36:18.770 --> 00:36:21.240
he fights with a submissive boxing style.

00:36:21.640 --> 00:36:24.380
Yeah. It's a first for me,

00:36:24.380 --> 00:36:25.850
to see him fight so aggressively

00:36:25.850 --> 00:36:27.610
risking it all like this.

00:36:29.650 --> 00:36:31.250
Kimura.

00:36:31.450 --> 00:36:35.520
I know why you fight so hard.

00:36:35.660 --> 00:36:38.660
As boxers we're always at the edge of the cliff.

00:36:38.660 --> 00:36:39.960
While everyone rises

00:36:39.960 --> 00:36:42.970
we're always stuck at the bottom.

00:36:43.400 --> 00:36:45.970
We have reasons for not holding back!

00:36:45.970 --> 00:36:48.000
Back off damn it!

00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:49.070
I won't back off.

00:36:49.070 --> 00:36:50.700
I'll never back off!

00:36:50.710 --> 00:36:53.240
Over the past 5 years in this world.

00:36:53.240 --> 00:36:55.480
I had no confidence or pride.

00:36:55.740 --> 00:36:59.480
But there's one thing very close to us.

00:36:59.980 --> 00:37:01.720
No matter what fight lay ahead

00:37:01.720 --> 00:37:05.550
a man who always stepped forward
until he became champion.

00:37:05.550 --> 00:37:08.490
With my own courage I won't lose.

00:37:08.920 --> 00:37:10.590
In the 7th round's second half,

00:37:10.590 --> 00:37:13.260
the challenger persistently attacks with body blows,

00:37:13.260 --> 00:37:15.630
while the champion is all defensive!

00:37:15.630 --> 00:37:17.500
Mashiba-san's guard is coming down.

00:37:18.170 --> 00:37:19.800
H-his jaw is...

00:37:21.960 --> 00:37:24.170
A rising Kimura call has erupted!

00:37:24.170 --> 00:37:26.340
Since being crowned as the Junior Lightweight king,

00:37:26.340 --> 00:37:28.930
this champion has never struggled in a match!

00:37:28.930 --> 00:37:30.480
He is behind on the points,

00:37:30.480 --> 00:37:32.430
but the hope for the victory is rising!

00:37:32.850 --> 00:37:34.350
D-dad!

00:37:34.350 --> 00:37:35.440
Yes.

00:37:35.850 --> 00:37:40.290
You've grown into a man worthy of such cheering.

00:37:40.290 --> 00:37:43.440
I am so proud of you.

00:37:44.440 --> 00:37:46.760
The 7th round has ended!

00:37:46.760 --> 00:37:48.830
You've fought well, Challenger!

00:37:48.830 --> 00:37:51.950
He'll continue using body blows in the next round.

00:37:52.530 --> 00:37:55.940
But your monotonous attack won't work on me.

00:37:55.940 --> 00:37:57.460
I'll show you.

00:37:57.460 --> 00:38:01.980
By now Mashiba's attention should
be drawn to his lower body.

00:38:02.880 --> 00:38:05.310
The stage is finally set.

00:38:06.310 --> 00:38:07.970
What's left is one more shot!

00:38:07.970 --> 00:38:09.250
5 years...

00:38:09.250 --> 00:38:10.680
It's been so long.

00:38:10.690 --> 00:38:12.970
I'll put everything into it.

00:38:12.970 --> 00:38:16.520
All my effort over the years will go into this one shot.

00:38:16.520 --> 00:38:17.860
I'll hit him hard with it!

00:38:20.480 --> 00:38:22.230
It's now the 8th round!

00:38:22.230 --> 00:38:23.930
The Kimura call still resounds throughout the hall!

00:38:23.930 --> 00:38:26.990
Now, who will receive the cruel verdict?

00:38:26.990 --> 00:38:28.340
I underestimated him.

00:38:28.340 --> 00:38:30.300
Since he has those kind of eyes

00:38:30.310 --> 00:38:32.450
I'll have to kill him with my best punches.

00:38:33.580 --> 00:38:35.740
Several times he must've lost his consciousness.

00:38:35.740 --> 00:38:37.460
Yet his eyes were always alive.

00:38:37.460 --> 00:38:39.960
But he's close to his limit.

00:38:40.420 --> 00:38:42.150
This round will be it!

00:38:42.850 --> 00:38:45.130
He's luring me.

00:38:45.130 --> 00:38:47.620
Fine, I'll bite.

00:38:47.620 --> 00:38:48.340
However...

00:38:50.760 --> 00:38:52.100
I'm using all my power!

00:38:52.530 --> 00:38:54.860
This left will bring me the World!

00:38:57.300 --> 00:38:58.500
He evaded it!

00:38:58.500 --> 00:39:00.350
Another left body explodes!

00:39:00.350 --> 00:39:02.360
He's got the timing down.

00:39:02.770 --> 00:39:04.360
Again, it's blocked!

00:39:06.240 --> 00:39:08.070
The challenger's jaw is blown back!

00:39:09.840 --> 00:39:11.820
But he returns with another body shot!

00:39:11.820 --> 00:39:13.580
I'll smash your jaw again!

00:39:16.690 --> 00:39:18.040
It was blocked again!

00:39:18.040 --> 00:39:19.650
Another uppercut explodes!

00:39:21.890 --> 00:39:23.420
How many...

00:39:23.430 --> 00:39:25.750
how many times have I punched the sand bag?

00:39:28.260 --> 00:39:29.560
A hundred...

00:39:29.560 --> 00:39:30.260
a thousand times...

00:39:30.670 --> 00:39:32.760
I've hit it!

00:39:37.210 --> 00:39:38.410
Everything...

00:39:39.810 --> 00:39:41.770
goes into this one shot!

00:39:59.960 --> 00:40:01.960
He's down!

00:40:01.960 --> 00:40:05.130
In the 8th round, the challenger
displayed a ferocious punch!

00:40:08.700 --> 00:40:11.010
Why am I looking at the ceiling?

00:40:13.010 --> 00:40:15.440
Am I down?

00:40:15.440 --> 00:40:17.010
How was I hit?

00:40:20.850 --> 00:40:22.950
Why am I down?

00:40:24.390 --> 00:40:26.390
I don't get it...

00:40:30.130 --> 00:40:30.780
Seven!

00:40:33.900 --> 00:40:36.000
The champion is up!

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:37.500
He got up...

00:40:37.500 --> 00:40:38.120
Eight!

00:40:38.300 --> 00:40:39.700
He's still shaking, Referee!

00:40:40.100 --> 00:40:41.710
I've taken my stance!

00:40:42.040 --> 00:40:43.070
Stop him.

00:40:43.070 --> 00:40:44.210
It's a close call.

00:40:48.210 --> 00:40:49.210
BOX!

00:40:49.210 --> 00:40:50.260
The match resumes!

00:40:50.260 --> 00:40:53.010
The 8th round is left with one minute!

00:40:53.010 --> 00:40:54.950
You're pretty good Champion.

00:40:54.950 --> 00:40:57.010
That was my best shot.

00:40:57.420 --> 00:40:58.790
If one shot doesn't do the job...

00:40:58.790 --> 00:41:01.020
I'll give you two or three more!

00:41:01.220 --> 00:41:02.730
That got him good, so finish him already!

00:41:03.120 --> 00:41:03.940
Tatsuya!

00:41:10.900 --> 00:41:12.600
Did that last punch come from above?

00:41:12.600 --> 00:41:13.990
I can't take another.

00:41:15.270 --> 00:41:16.570
He's guarding high!

00:41:17.470 --> 00:41:19.580
A left body blow connected!

00:41:19.970 --> 00:41:21.040
Damn it.

00:41:21.040 --> 00:41:22.840
He hits low just when I guard high.

00:41:22.840 --> 00:41:24.980
I can't tell what's coming next any more.

00:41:26.550 --> 00:41:29.790
The champion's Flicker stops the
challenger from closing in.

00:41:31.250 --> 00:41:33.150
With my right eye completely shut

00:41:33.150 --> 00:41:35.590
that bastard's left is so hard to see.

00:41:36.520 --> 00:41:37.590
Who cares.

00:41:37.590 --> 00:41:38.800
Charge!

00:41:39.330 --> 00:41:41.560
The challenger uses his shoulder to charge in!

00:41:41.560 --> 00:41:43.760
Your punch can't get me here!

00:41:44.470 --> 00:41:45.530
He's guarding high.

00:41:45.530 --> 00:41:46.530
Low then.

00:41:46.530 --> 00:41:49.270
I'll hit him until he drops his guard!

00:41:50.940 --> 00:41:53.570
The challenger attacks with
fierce blows to the body.

00:41:53.840 --> 00:41:55.680
The champion is pushed into the ropes!

00:42:06.250 --> 00:42:08.560
The champion's guard has gone down!

00:42:08.560 --> 00:42:09.130
It's open!

00:42:17.230 --> 00:42:18.840
If I get hit again...

00:42:19.270 --> 00:42:20.630
everything will end.

00:42:25.010 --> 00:42:26.570
lose everything!

00:42:29.680 --> 00:42:31.550
Brother...

00:42:31.550 --> 00:42:34.820
what are we going to do... from now on?

00:42:35.520 --> 00:42:37.050
Shut up.

00:42:37.650 --> 00:42:38.820
Don't cry, Kumi.

00:42:39.920 --> 00:42:41.320
Don't cry.

00:42:42.690 --> 00:42:45.730
The challenger's powerful right explodes!

00:42:45.730 --> 00:42:46.540
Brother!

00:42:46.760 --> 00:42:48.790
Dragon Fish Blow number 2!

00:42:49.200 --> 00:42:50.160
No...

00:42:51.700 --> 00:42:53.530
I don't want...

00:42:54.470 --> 00:42:56.940
to lose everything.

00:42:58.040 --> 00:42:59.670
Damn it...

00:43:01.040 --> 00:43:04.010
I can't lose here!

00:43:04.010 --> 00:43:05.520
Brother!

00:43:08.880 --> 00:43:10.780
The champion is not going down!

00:43:10.790 --> 00:43:12.230
It's a desperate clinch!

00:43:12.230 --> 00:43:13.950
That was a clean hit!

00:43:13.960 --> 00:43:16.260
Mashiba doesn't take hits well.

00:43:16.260 --> 00:43:18.330
He should be way past his limit already.

00:43:18.330 --> 00:43:19.390
He can still hang on?

00:43:20.660 --> 00:43:22.300
This isn't about skill.

00:43:22.300 --> 00:43:23.240
What makes Mashiba scary...

00:43:23.770 --> 00:43:25.770
is his desperation for victory.

00:43:27.270 --> 00:43:29.370
Get off, damn it!

00:43:30.170 --> 00:43:31.670
Mashiba, let go.

00:43:31.670 --> 00:43:32.460
Break it!

00:43:32.460 --> 00:43:34.040
Stop that!

00:43:34.040 --> 00:43:35.480
Get off now!

00:43:35.480 --> 00:43:37.010
What a lousy champion!

00:43:37.010 --> 00:43:38.010
Referee.

00:43:38.010 --> 00:43:39.220
Deduct a point, a point!

00:43:39.580 --> 00:43:40.510
Don't let go, Mashiba!

00:43:40.520 --> 00:43:41.430
Hang in there!

00:43:41.850 --> 00:43:43.120
Mashiba, break it!

00:43:43.120 --> 00:43:44.180
Or I'll deduct a point!

00:43:44.180 --> 00:43:45.890
Why you...

00:43:49.590 --> 00:43:52.330
The 8th round ends!

00:43:52.330 --> 00:43:54.560
That was another impressive
round for the challenger!

00:43:54.560 --> 00:43:57.400
The champion barely made it through!

00:43:57.800 --> 00:43:58.900
That was close.

00:43:58.900 --> 00:44:00.900
If he didn't clinch...

00:44:00.900 --> 00:44:03.140
No, he's good.

00:44:03.140 --> 00:44:06.310
He's really an incredible champion.

00:44:06.310 --> 00:44:09.660
At that time, I sensed a great determination.

00:44:10.080 --> 00:44:11.050
That's right.

00:44:11.050 --> 00:44:12.780
The champion's still determined.

00:44:12.780 --> 00:44:14.170
Don't let your guard down despite your advantage.

00:44:15.280 --> 00:44:18.170
This looks bad, he's really hurt.

00:44:19.750 --> 00:44:22.560
Listen, watch out for his high-low variation.

00:44:22.560 --> 00:44:23.920
Tighten your guard and...

00:44:23.930 --> 00:44:25.090
Can you hear me?

00:44:29.530 --> 00:44:30.900
SECONDS OUT!

00:44:31.900 --> 00:44:33.700
H-hey, Mashiba!

00:44:33.700 --> 00:44:36.470
I don't want... to lose...

00:44:36.470 --> 00:44:37.190
Mashiba...

00:44:37.640 --> 00:44:39.940
Alright, go get him!

00:44:39.940 --> 00:44:40.910
Just now...

00:44:41.980 --> 00:44:44.200
I could see the belt!

00:44:48.920 --> 00:44:51.250
I'll return as the champion.

00:44:51.490 --> 00:44:52.950
Round 9!

00:44:56.360 --> 00:44:57.760
One more shot!

00:44:57.760 --> 00:44:59.430
With my Dragon Fish Blow

00:44:59.430 --> 00:45:00.710
he will definitely go down!

00:45:01.130 --> 00:45:03.360
I can't let him continue like this.

00:45:03.370 --> 00:45:04.630
If I don't survive this,

00:45:04.630 --> 00:45:06.220
the World is out of the question!

00:45:08.170 --> 00:45:10.430
The champion attacks with a rare right!

00:45:10.870 --> 00:45:12.110
He's using his right!

00:45:12.870 --> 00:45:14.310
I'll admit that...

00:45:14.340 --> 00:45:17.270
you're the best challenger!

00:45:19.810 --> 00:45:21.620
A right in full-swing.

00:45:21.620 --> 00:45:22.690
He wants to finish it.

00:45:23.280 --> 00:45:25.200
He's trying to regain control of the match.

00:45:25.620 --> 00:45:27.280
That's just what I need.

00:45:27.690 --> 00:45:29.320
Both of my eyes are about shut.

00:45:29.320 --> 00:45:30.290
I can't gauge the distance any more.

00:45:30.860 --> 00:45:32.690
Bring it on!

00:45:33.900 --> 00:45:35.260
In the ring's center...

00:45:35.260 --> 00:45:36.750
a vicious exchange breaks out!

00:45:36.750 --> 00:45:40.100
This must be their last burst of energy!

00:45:42.800 --> 00:45:45.440
Kimura's betting his life as boxer on this!

00:45:45.440 --> 00:45:48.510
Show him the power of desperation!

00:45:48.740 --> 00:45:51.750
Show him the difference in scale of your dreams!

00:45:53.180 --> 00:45:54.930
He swings with his right!

00:45:57.690 --> 00:45:59.490
That powerful shot was effective!

00:46:02.190 --> 00:46:04.530
Knocking him upwards is an uppercut!

00:46:05.660 --> 00:46:08.820
This is the champion's winning pattern!

00:46:08.820 --> 00:46:09.530
Damn it!

00:46:09.530 --> 00:46:11.490
Go down.

00:46:29.580 --> 00:46:31.390
Wow, he retaliated!

00:46:33.720 --> 00:46:36.160
The challenger advances swiftly.

00:46:36.890 --> 00:46:38.860
H-he'll be fine, Kumi-chan.

00:46:38.860 --> 00:46:40.790
Mashiba will definitely win.

00:46:40.800 --> 00:46:43.480
My brother is cowering away.

00:46:44.300 --> 00:46:46.630
Always acting strong,

00:46:46.630 --> 00:46:48.100
he's now cowering away.

00:46:48.100 --> 00:46:50.200
I've never seen him like that.

00:46:50.210 --> 00:46:51.540
Ever.

00:46:52.310 --> 00:46:54.410
I can't overcome the damage.

00:46:54.880 --> 00:46:57.210
My body doesn't move like I want it to.

00:46:57.910 --> 00:47:00.580
Damn it he's good.

00:47:00.580 --> 00:47:02.960
Really good!

00:47:02.960 --> 00:47:04.520
The champion clinches!

00:47:05.620 --> 00:47:07.350
But he read ahead!

00:47:07.360 --> 00:47:09.220
He evades it and slams in body blows repeatedly!

00:47:10.430 --> 00:47:11.930
He looks seriously hurt!

00:47:13.190 --> 00:47:15.500
The challenger comes closer to the belt!

00:47:15.500 --> 00:47:17.890
His enthronement is right before him!

00:47:19.300 --> 00:47:20.100
Now!

00:47:24.860 --> 00:47:26.070
No!

00:47:26.070 --> 00:47:28.640
I don't want to lose!

00:47:28.640 --> 00:47:29.360
I see it!

00:47:30.010 --> 00:47:31.150
The belt!

00:47:31.150 --> 00:47:32.620
When this arm is fully extended

00:47:32.620 --> 00:47:33.870
it is within reach!

00:47:33.870 --> 00:47:36.370
I can't lose!

00:47:36.370 --> 00:47:39.390
Reach for it!

00:47:43.430 --> 00:47:44.430
I've reached it!

00:47:54.900 --> 00:47:56.270
Why?

00:47:57.870 --> 00:47:59.410
I reached out...

00:48:00.580 --> 00:48:02.210
but it's all dark.

00:48:03.810 --> 00:48:05.510
Belt and all...

00:48:06.770 --> 00:48:08.380
can't be seen.

00:48:10.740 --> 00:48:12.280
Kimura!

00:48:14.690 --> 00:48:17.520
What a nerve-wrecking simultaneous
exchange of rights!

00:48:17.530 --> 00:48:19.660
But, the emergent winner is the champion!

00:48:19.660 --> 00:48:21.800
It's a devastating down!

00:48:21.800 --> 00:48:24.670
The look of disbelief on the champion...

00:48:24.670 --> 00:48:27.130
speaks of that simultaneous exchange's intensity.

00:48:28.140 --> 00:48:29.800
T-Tatsuya!

00:48:30.570 --> 00:48:32.010
Damn it!

00:48:32.010 --> 00:48:33.470
It was so damn close.

00:48:33.910 --> 00:48:35.010
Get the towel.

00:48:35.010 --> 00:48:35.720
Yes.

00:48:36.340 --> 00:48:38.150
Is it over?

00:48:38.150 --> 00:48:40.220
The one who connected first won.

00:48:41.080 --> 00:48:43.050
Kimura's arching punch...

00:48:43.050 --> 00:48:44.730
and Mashiba's straight punch...

00:48:45.150 --> 00:48:47.220
the difference in lines decided it.

00:48:47.220 --> 00:48:48.160
That can't be.

00:48:48.160 --> 00:48:50.230
The match isn't over yet!

00:48:50.530 --> 00:48:51.990
Right against right, it was a counter.

00:48:51.990 --> 00:48:53.630
Can he really get up?

00:48:56.130 --> 00:48:57.970
Hey hold on, Shinoda-san.

00:48:57.970 --> 00:48:59.170
What do you want?

00:48:59.170 --> 00:49:01.700
You saw how dangerously he fell!

00:49:01.900 --> 00:49:05.840
But, he decided that this is his last match.

00:49:05.840 --> 00:49:08.710
Let him finish it on his own terms.

00:49:09.110 --> 00:49:10.680
I feel that way too.

00:49:10.680 --> 00:49:12.910
But if this leads to something irreparable,

00:49:12.910 --> 00:49:13.470
what will you do?

00:49:19.990 --> 00:49:20.740
Seven!

00:49:22.560 --> 00:49:23.790
No way.

00:49:23.790 --> 00:49:24.690
That's impossible...

00:49:25.190 --> 00:49:25.910
Eight!

00:49:28.440 --> 00:49:30.960
H-he stood up!

00:49:30.970 --> 00:49:32.430
Was it his determination to win the title?

00:49:32.430 --> 00:49:33.950
Or was it some wild instinct?

00:49:33.950 --> 00:49:36.600
What motivates the challenger?

00:49:36.600 --> 00:49:38.640
Kimura, let me see your eyes.

00:49:39.610 --> 00:49:41.580
The referee checks out his condition.

00:49:42.580 --> 00:49:44.080
How will he call it?

00:49:44.080 --> 00:49:45.160
Will it resume?

00:49:45.380 --> 00:49:47.080
Or will it stop?

00:49:49.780 --> 00:49:51.880
Please, let him continue.

00:49:52.290 --> 00:49:53.850
Let him carry on, Referee!

00:49:53.860 --> 00:49:55.190
Let it continue!

00:49:55.190 --> 00:49:57.220
Yeah, let it continue!

00:50:03.930 --> 00:50:05.230
Stop it, Referee!

00:50:07.670 --> 00:50:10.230
Let him fight until the very end!

00:50:11.210 --> 00:50:11.940
BOX!

00:50:11.940 --> 00:50:13.940
It resumes!

00:50:15.840 --> 00:50:18.650
N-no matter how many times...

00:50:18.650 --> 00:50:21.950
No matter how many times I knock
him down, he keeps getting up.

00:50:22.350 --> 00:50:25.120
I need to kill him off completely!

00:50:27.820 --> 00:50:29.420
He's charging in desperately,

00:50:30.040 --> 00:50:32.160
out of fear and panic!

00:50:32.160 --> 00:50:34.930
That Mashiba-san is... scared.

00:50:41.440 --> 00:50:42.640
If I lose...

00:50:43.470 --> 00:50:44.770
I will retire.

00:50:45.560 --> 00:50:46.570
Kimura!

00:50:46.570 --> 00:50:47.560
Win!

00:50:51.080 --> 00:50:52.020
Kimura-san!

00:50:55.740 --> 00:50:59.190
Go!

00:51:05.630 --> 00:51:06.490
Stop!

00:51:06.490 --> 00:51:08.660
The referee stops the champion!

00:51:08.660 --> 00:51:10.000
What's going on?

00:51:32.890 --> 00:51:35.690
He's no longer conscious.

00:51:39.490 --> 00:51:41.780
The match is over!

00:51:42.200 --> 00:51:45.100
With the challenger frozen with his fist extended,

00:51:45.100 --> 00:51:47.290
the gong sounds to signal the end of the match!

00:51:47.700 --> 00:51:51.270
The death match is finally over!

00:51:52.610 --> 00:51:53.770
Kimura!

00:51:54.240 --> 00:51:55.610
Kimura-san!

00:51:55.610 --> 00:51:57.000
Wait up, Ippo!

00:52:01.580 --> 00:52:02.220
Mashiba.

00:52:03.950 --> 00:52:07.350
His sweat is so cold.

00:52:08.620 --> 00:52:12.060
If that punch followed through

00:52:12.860 --> 00:52:14.400
I could have been...

00:52:15.500 --> 00:52:16.330
Kimura.

00:52:16.330 --> 00:52:19.270
Shinoda-san, he's still fighting.

00:52:19.270 --> 00:52:23.000
He doesn't know that the match is over,

00:52:23.000 --> 00:52:25.310
so he can't withdraw his fist.

00:52:25.310 --> 00:52:27.640
He's still fighting!

00:52:34.580 --> 00:52:35.460
Kimura...

00:52:44.360 --> 00:52:45.470
It's all right now.

00:52:45.860 --> 00:52:47.290
It's over.

00:52:47.300 --> 00:52:48.530
You did well.

00:52:49.360 --> 00:52:51.480
I-it's over?

00:52:52.330 --> 00:52:53.800
It's over...

00:53:02.480 --> 00:53:05.980
Kimura! Kimura!

00:53:13.790 --> 00:53:15.160
D-dad...

00:53:15.160 --> 00:53:16.620
Yeah.

00:53:16.620 --> 00:53:18.390
You did well, Tatsuya.

00:53:18.390 --> 00:53:20.960
Till the very end, you did well.

00:53:20.960 --> 00:53:23.010
You were just great.

00:53:23.770 --> 00:53:25.570
You're the best son.

00:53:29.200 --> 00:53:30.470
Mashiba, wait up.

00:53:31.070 --> 00:53:33.470
There's still the winner's interview and stuff.

00:53:33.480 --> 00:53:35.110
Winner?

00:53:35.110 --> 00:53:37.040
It was a K.0. victory!

00:53:38.780 --> 00:53:40.880
If I stayed as the winner,

00:53:40.880 --> 00:53:42.520
I'd only be humiliated.

00:54:03.410 --> 00:54:05.070
Takamura-san.

00:54:05.070 --> 00:54:06.440
Aoki.

00:54:06.440 --> 00:54:07.780
Ippo.

00:54:07.780 --> 00:54:09.110
Shinoda-san.

00:54:09.110 --> 00:54:10.580
Yagi-san.

00:54:10.580 --> 00:54:11.550
Coach.

00:54:16.420 --> 00:54:17.480
As of today,

00:54:19.690 --> 00:54:20.940
I have retired.

00:54:26.460 --> 00:54:29.200
For all the days at the gym I really...

00:54:29.200 --> 00:54:30.950
thank you!

00:54:31.570 --> 00:54:34.450
Thank you very much!

00:54:39.410 --> 00:54:41.040
I've thought it through.

00:54:42.540 --> 00:54:46.750
I will never step into the ring as a fighter again.

00:55:00.800 --> 00:55:02.030
See ya.

00:55:11.740 --> 00:55:12.660
I'm heading out.

00:55:13.480 --> 00:55:15.640
Will you be okay?

00:55:15.640 --> 00:55:18.850
I'm just gonna drop by the gym.

00:55:18.850 --> 00:55:20.780
Hey, Tatsuya.

00:55:20.780 --> 00:55:24.320
Isn't it still early to know the names of flowers?

00:55:25.620 --> 00:55:28.090
We're still doing fine.

00:55:28.090 --> 00:55:30.180
You shouldn't quit...

00:55:32.660 --> 00:55:34.220
I've made up my mind.

00:55:35.230 --> 00:55:36.680
I see...

00:55:39.500 --> 00:55:42.070
It feels rather lonely.

00:55:42.070 --> 00:55:44.610
There's no time to sulk.

00:55:44.610 --> 00:55:47.370
You've seen many others retire.

00:55:47.380 --> 00:55:49.240
Even so...

00:55:49.240 --> 00:55:51.480
Kimura fought well.

00:55:51.480 --> 00:55:54.580
And, he's now at his new starting-line.

00:55:54.580 --> 00:55:56.250
Send him off with a smile.

00:55:56.480 --> 00:55:57.920
You're right.

00:55:57.920 --> 00:55:59.050
Yes.

00:55:59.050 --> 00:56:00.150
Show some guts,

00:56:00.160 --> 00:56:02.460
to fill in for Kimura's absence!

00:56:02.860 --> 00:56:04.860
Kimura's absence...

00:56:10.330 --> 00:56:11.970
Yeah!

00:56:15.640 --> 00:56:17.200
Our guts...

00:56:17.210 --> 00:56:19.770
Takamura-san actually misses him, too.

00:56:19.770 --> 00:56:22.280
Ippo, you too!

00:56:22.280 --> 00:56:23.640
O-Okay!

00:56:27.780 --> 00:56:32.320
That makes my retirement feel real.

00:56:35.820 --> 00:56:37.950
Wanpo, spelt in Katakana...

00:56:38.730 --> 00:56:40.830
I'm glad that you've got a name.

00:56:40.830 --> 00:56:43.260
I won't be seeing you very much anymore.

00:56:45.800 --> 00:56:46.700
Take care.

00:56:50.410 --> 00:56:52.510
What should I do now?

00:56:53.110 --> 00:56:56.940
For 5 years, I was drowned in boxing.

00:56:58.150 --> 00:57:00.010
I'll do the stuff I've been wanting to do.

00:57:04.550 --> 00:57:06.490
What would that be?

00:57:11.390 --> 00:57:12.560
NO!

00:57:12.560 --> 00:57:14.190
Not boxing!

00:57:15.060 --> 00:57:17.530
I did my best.

00:57:17.530 --> 00:57:19.530
I did so much of it.

00:57:21.700 --> 00:57:23.600
It was so close.

00:57:23.610 --> 00:57:26.240
If I stretched my fist out a little more.

00:57:27.380 --> 00:57:29.540
10 cm more...

00:57:29.540 --> 00:57:32.050
or was it 3 cm?

00:57:32.880 --> 00:57:34.750
3 cm...

00:57:34.750 --> 00:57:37.080
only that much of a difference.

00:57:38.190 --> 00:57:40.520
That's it?

00:57:40.520 --> 00:57:42.990
Why couldn't I do it?

00:57:44.430 --> 00:57:46.560
It was only...

00:57:46.560 --> 00:57:49.900
It was only 3 cm, yet I...

00:57:49.900 --> 00:57:51.030
I didn't have enough!

00:57:51.830 --> 00:57:54.130
I'll regret it...

00:57:54.140 --> 00:57:55.940
forever.

00:57:55.940 --> 00:58:00.640
I'll regret not making that extra 3 cm forever!

00:58:00.640 --> 00:58:04.040
Just 3 cm and regretting it forever...

00:58:09.180 --> 00:58:10.420
No!

00:58:12.490 --> 00:58:14.760
I don't want that!

00:58:19.260 --> 00:58:20.720
Kimura-san!

00:58:21.660 --> 00:58:22.220
Yo.

00:58:22.600 --> 00:58:23.700
Kimura!

00:58:23.700 --> 00:58:25.670
You, didn't you retire?

00:58:25.670 --> 00:58:27.400
Yes, I retired.

00:58:27.400 --> 00:58:29.270
Then, why?

00:58:29.270 --> 00:58:31.670
Kimura Tatsuya retired.

00:58:31.670 --> 00:58:32.640
But...

00:58:35.810 --> 00:58:37.310
Since when?

00:58:37.310 --> 00:58:38.740
K-Kimura?

00:58:39.150 --> 00:58:41.740
With my name in Katakana, I'll re-debut.

00:58:45.390 --> 00:58:47.050
That's the way it is...

00:58:47.060 --> 00:58:48.420
so watch over me again!

00:58:49.090 --> 00:58:50.190
Hell yeah!

00:58:50.190 --> 00:58:51.590
Kimura-san!

00:58:51.590 --> 00:58:54.190
But you've retired!

00:58:54.200 --> 00:58:55.260
You sure about this, old man?!

00:58:55.930 --> 00:58:57.260
It can't be helped.

00:58:57.770 --> 00:58:59.430
Damn you!

00:58:59.430 --> 00:59:01.260
Quit, damn it!

00:59:04.370 --> 00:59:05.270
Could it be...

00:59:10.850 --> 00:59:12.280
K-Kumi-san!

00:59:14.280 --> 00:59:16.920
Congratulations for your brother's victory.

00:59:16.920 --> 00:59:18.820
Umm, well... that's...

00:59:19.550 --> 00:59:20.820
Is Kimura-san...

00:59:22.740 --> 00:59:25.660
Kimura-san was going to retire,

00:59:25.660 --> 00:59:28.000
but he couldn't quit boxing, and came back.

00:59:31.070 --> 00:59:34.800
U-umm, Kumi-san, why are you here today?

00:59:35.840 --> 00:59:38.570
Well since my brother won,

00:59:38.570 --> 00:59:40.610
I was concerned about Kimura-san.

00:59:44.410 --> 00:59:45.150
How's that?

00:59:45.150 --> 00:59:48.950
I'll really quit!

01:00:03.500 --> 01:00:07.840
It's always the same no matter what I do

01:00:08.300 --> 01:00:16.810
I make the same mistake over and over

01:00:17.310 --> 01:00:23.780
What is really important?

01:00:24.150 --> 01:00:26.490
Tracing my steps

01:00:26.790 --> 01:00:30.760
I keep looking down

01:00:30.990 --> 01:00:33.990
At times like this

01:00:34.260 --> 01:00:37.630
I try looking up

01:00:37.830 --> 01:00:41.100
I try looking in the distance

01:00:41.140 --> 01:00:47.640
I find a different outlook

01:00:48.080 --> 01:00:54.710
When I look up at the narrow path

01:00:55.250 --> 01:01:02.060
The world opens up 360 degrees wide
